            "description": "",
            "summary": "The tariff will apply starting Dec. 26 to about C$10 billion ($7.1 billion) of imported products including wind towers, prefabricated buildings, fasteners and wires.  It marks the first time Carney has added new import taxes to US products since he dropped most of Canada\u2019s retaliatory tariffs in September.  A broad 25% tariff on US steel and aluminum remains, and the prime minister has resisted calls to match US President Donald Trump\u2019s 50% levy on those metals.",
